## 9. Conditional and NULL Functions

```sql
SELECT IF(80>=50,'Pass','Fail');
SELECT IFNULL(NULL,0);
SELECT COALESCE(NULL,NULL,'Available');

-- Student grade calculation
SELECT StudentName, Marks,
CASE
    WHEN Marks>=90 THEN 'A'
    WHEN Marks>=75 THEN 'B'
    WHEN Marks>=50 THEN 'C'
    ELSE 'Fail'
END AS Grade
FROM Student;
```

## 10. Sorting, Grouping and Limiting

```sql
-- Sort employees by salary
SELECT * FROM Employee ORDER BY Salary DESC;

-- Group staff by department
SELECT Department, COUNT(*) AS TotalStaff
FROM Staff
GROUP BY Department;

-- Departments having more than one staff member
SELECT Department, COUNT(*) AS TotalStaff
FROM Staff
GROUP BY Department
HAVING COUNT(*)>1;

-- Display first five products
SELECT * FROM Product LIMIT 5;
```

## Conclusion

This assignment covers arithmetic, comparison, logical and special operators; string, numeric, aggregate, date, conditional and NULL functions; and sorting, grouping and limiting in MySQL.
